\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Plunged in a gulf of dark despair
\par We wretched sinners lay,
\par Without one cheerful beam of hope,
\par Or spark of glimmering day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. With pitying eyes the Prince of Peace
\par Beheld our helpless grief;
\par He saw, and- O amazing love!
\par He flew to our relief.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Down from the shining seats above
\par With joyful haste He sped,
\par Entered the grave in mortal flesh,
\par And dwelt among the dead.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. O for this love let rocks and hills 
\par Their lasting silence break,
\par And all harmonious human tongues
\par The Saviour's praises speak!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Angels, assist our mighty joys,
\par Strike all your harps of gold;
\par But when you raise your highest notes,
\par His love can ne'er be told.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

